            {'text':'The manager reviewed the log, she called the technician immediately.','task':'Choose the revision that shows two separate complete actions without adding a new logical relationship.','choices':['The manager reviewed the log; she called the technician immediately.','The manager reviewed the log, she called the technician immediately.','The manager reviewed the log: because she called the technician immediately.','The manager reviewed; the log she called the technician immediately.'],'answer':'A. The manager reviewed the log; she called the technician immediately.','why':'A semicolon correctly joins the two closely related independent clauses without inventing cause or contrast.'},
            {'text':'The notice includes {{blank}} a map, a phone number, and office hours.','task':'Should a colon go in the blank?','choices':['No punctuation is needed.','Use a colon.','Use a semicolon.','Use a period.'],'answer':'A. No punctuation is needed.','why':'The words before the blank do not form a complete clause; the verb includes flows directly into its objects.'},
